    "title": "Invaluable lessons at DA's Office | Letters To Editor | ellsworthamerican.com",
    "text": "To the Editor:\nThis past summer, I had the opportunity to experience the full lifecycle of Maine’s criminal legal system firsthand as an intern at the Hancock County District Attorney’s Office. My experience, which saw me move across office desks, courtrooms and the front lines of Maine’s law enforcement networks, is one that I encourage any students in Hancock County who are interested in learning more about the legal field to seek out.",
